@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Deploying to Azure App Services";
    ViewData["ActiveMenu"] = "AzureDevOps";
}

<div class="container py-4">
    <p class="lead text-center">Learn how to deploy web applications to Azure App Services efficiently using Azure DevOps.</p>
    <hr />

    <!-- Introduction -->
    <div class="mt-4">
        <h2 class="text-success">What is Azure App Services?</h2>
        <p>
            Azure App Services is a fully managed platform-as-a-service (PaaS) offering for building, deploying, and scaling web applications. It supports multiple programming languages such as .NET, Java, Node.js, Python, PHP, and Ruby.
        </p>
        <p>
            With built-in security, auto-scaling, and integration with Azure DevOps, Azure App Services is a preferred choice for cloud-based applications.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/azure-app-services.jpg" alt="Azure App Services Overview" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure App Services simplifies application deployment and scaling.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Deployment Methods -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-warning">Deployment Methods</h2>
        <p>Azure App Services supports multiple deployment methods, including:</p>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Azure DevOps Pipelines:</strong> Automate CI/CD for seamless deployments.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>FTP/SFTP:</strong> Upload files manually to the server.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Local Git:</strong> Push code directly from a local Git repository.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>GitHub Actions:</strong> Deploy using GitHub-based workflows.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Docker Containers:</strong> Deploy containerized applications to App Services.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/deployment-methods.jpg" alt="Deployment Methods" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Various deployment options are available based on application needs.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Step-by-Step Deployment Guide -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-danger">Step-by-Step Deployment Guide</h2>
        <ol class="list-group list-group-numbered">
            <li class="list-group-item">Login to the <strong>Azure Portal</strong> and navigate to "App Services".</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Click on "Create App Service" and configure the app settings.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Select the appropriate runtime, region, and service plan.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Once created, go to the "Deployment Center" to set up deployment.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Choose your preferred source control (Azure Repos, GitHub, Bitbucket, etc.).</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Configure Continuous Deployment settings for automatic deployments.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item">Click "Save" and trigger the first deployment.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/deployment-steps.jpg" alt="Deployment Steps" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Setting up deployment in Azure App Services.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Best Practices -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-info">Best Practices for Azure App Services Deployment</h2>
        <ul class="list-group list-group-flush">
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Enable Auto-Scaling:</strong> Scale applications dynamically based on traffic.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Use Deployment Slots:</strong> Test changes in staging before moving to production.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Implement CI/CD:</strong> Automate builds and releases using Azure Pipelines.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Monitor Performance:</strong> Use Application Insights to track app performance.</li>
            <li class="list-group-item"><strong>Secure Your App:</strong> Configure authentication and authorization settings.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/best-practices.jpg" alt="Best Practices" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Following best practices ensures smooth and secure deployments.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Conclusion -->
    <div class="mt-5">
        <h2 class="text-secondary">Conclusion</h2>
        <p>
            Deploying applications to Azure App Services provides a robust, scalable, and secure environment for hosting modern applications. By leveraging DevOps best practices, automated deployments, and monitoring tools, teams can achieve seamless application delivery and maintain high availability.
        </p>
        <div class="text-center my-3">
            <img src="https://example.com/conclusion.jpg" alt="Azure App Services Summary" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-lg w-100">
            <p class="text-muted mt-2"><small>Azure App Services enables rapid and reliable application deployments.</small></p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
